put ","type":"text"},{"code":"Position","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to the layer’s transform. When released near the center, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"card snaps back to its resting position.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Interaction_DragView","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_DragView","role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_dragview"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","abstract":[{"text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s ","type":"text"},{"code":".origami","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example.","type":"text"}],"title":"Swami","url":"\/documentation\/swami","type":"topic","role":"collection"}}}